From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] uxtheme: XP's minimum part size and caption text without an icon

Purpose: match two details of XP's uxtheme and caption in the XP shell
session.
Windows behavior: GetThemePartSize with TS_MIN gives the part's content
margins, at least 1 (Luna's header item: 3x1 with hh.exe), as Windows 7
does; a caption without an icon starts its text two pixels further in (a
message box on the reference XP machine).
Wine before: TS_MIN gave the image's size; the text started at the
frame and two pixels.
Change: the version 4 rule for TS_MIN also for XP's styles in the XP
shell session; two more pixels before the title without an icon.
Evidence: hh.exe gives XP's sizes; xpcmp.exe's message box caption is
pixel-identical.
Scope: the XP shell session (WIN4WINE_EXTERNAL_SHELL, no WIN4WINE_SHELL).
---
 dlls/uxtheme/draw.c   | 5 +++--
 dlls/uxtheme/window.c | 4 ++++
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/uxtheme/draw.c b/dlls/uxtheme/draw.c
index ce3be62..770c6c3 100644
--- a/dlls/uxtheme/draw.c
+++ b/dlls/uxtheme/draw.c
@@ -937,8 +937,9 @@ static HRESULT get_image_part_size(HTHEME hTheme, int iPartId, int iStateId, REC
         }
         case TS_MIN:
             /* Windows 7 (a version 4 style): the content margins, at least 1
-             * (Explorer sizes its address and search bands from it) */
-            if (MSSTYLES_ActiveThemeFormat4())
+             * (Explorer sizes its address and search bands from it); XP SP3
+             * too, in the XP shell (Luna's header item: 3x1 with hh.exe) */
+            if (MSSTYLES_ActiveThemeFormat4() || win4wine_shell() == WIN4WINE_SHELL_XP)
             {
                 MARGINS margins = {0};
                 GetThemeMargins(hTheme, NULL, iPartId, iStateId, TMT_CONTENTMARGINS, NULL, &margins);
diff --git a/dlls/uxtheme/window.c b/dlls/uxtheme/window.c
index 914cb80..695ba82 100644
--- a/dlls/uxtheme/window.c
+++ b/dlls/uxtheme/window.c
@@ -571,6 +571,10 @@ static BOOL draw_non_client(HWND hwnd, HDC target, BOOL paint)
                    icon, width, height, 0, NULL, DI_NORMAL);
         text.left += width + 4;
     }
+    /* XP starts the title two pixels further in without an icon (a message
+     * box's, compared with the reference XP machine) */
+    else if (win4wine_shell() == WIN4WINE_SHELL_XP)
+        text.left += 2;
     if (style & WS_SYSMENU)
     {
         POINT cursor;
